My brand new MD-9600 - - Serial : 2401A0xxx - 2571 Sticker on side (Whatever that is)<br>Was loaded with HW V5 firmware, that seems to function well.<br><br>I'm quite sure my radio also showed as HW V2.xx , in the original CPS info.<br>But i think my original version info said it was written w. CP(S) version 1.27.<br><br><br>I was collecting "Original FW" files from here, before the upgrade.<br><a href="https://www.passion-radio.fr/mobile-vhf-uhf/md9600-505.html" class="postlink">https://www.passion-radio.fr/mobile-vhf ... 0-505.html</a><br><a href="https://www.radioddity.com/pages/tyt-download" class="postlink">https://www.radioddity.com/pages/tyt-download</a><br><a href="https://www.tyt888.com/Download.html" class="postlink">https://www.tyt888.com/Download.html</a><br><br>My conversion steps<br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/viewtopic.php?f=18&amp;t=4211&amp;p=31946#p32001" class="postlink">viewtopic.php?f=18&amp;t=4211&amp;p=31946#p32001</a><br><strong class="text-strong">Pay attention to the backups,</strong> to be taken immediately after the opengd77 fw has been loaded into the radio.<br><br><br>Top - post in MD9600 conversion thread - This is the "reference"<br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/viewtopic.php?f=18&amp;t=2035#p17115" class="postlink">viewtopic.php?f=18&amp;t=2035#p17115</a><br><br><br>I used this donor file<br>Download the Official firmware to act as the "donor" for the DMR codec <a href="https://www.passion-radio.com/index.php?controller=attachment&amp;id_attachment=760" class="postlink">https://www.passion-radio.com/index.php ... chment=760</a><br>Unzip the donor firmware zip file, to extract the donor file MD9600-CSV(2571V5)-V26.45.bin<br>Note. This file is the same for all MD9600 hardware versions.<br><br>.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5917">OZ1FTG</a> — Sun Jul 07, 2024 8:00 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
